WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.300
Inside multiply, the block loads left and right tiles into shared memory.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.520
After the barrier, each output thread accumulates products using those tiles.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:19.125
The second barrier prevents the next load from overwriting a tile while another thread still reads it. main defines width, tile and the two-dimensional launch.

00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:21.755
Load tiles.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.210
Threads fill shared left and right arrays.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.830
Reuse operands.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.920
Several outputs consume the same tile values.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.225
Protect reuse.

00:00:30.225 --> 00:00:33.215
Synchronise before loading the next tiles.

00:00:34.715 --> 00:00:39.760
Threads reuse shared tiles while each output sum is working state associated with its thread.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:45.670
This multiply kernel uses scalar arithmetic; it does not call matrix-unit instructions.
